{"id":3798,"date":"2017-06-18T11:48:44","date_gmt":"2017-06-18T15:48:44","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=3798"},"modified":"2017-06-18T11:48:44","modified_gmt":"2017-06-18T15:48:44","slug":"honoring-our-veterans-at-the-park","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/06\/18\/honoring-our-veterans-at-the-park\/","title":{"rendered":"Honoring Our Veterans at The Park"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>This post is late &#8230; we&#8217;ve been having too much fun here outside and have not been up to date on posting pictures to the blog.<\/p>\n<p>I wanted to share with you how we were all able to honor our Veterans here at the park a few weeks ago on the Memorial Day holiday weekend.<\/p>\n<p>Last year, the association bought a new aluminum flagpole and it was installed last fall. \u00a0This spring flowers were planted at the base of the pole and on Saturday May 27th, we all gathered around, dedicated the new American Flag and honored residents (and visitors) of the park who have served protecting our freedoms.<\/p>\n<p>The Veteran&#8217;s names were called out along with their branch of service, their rank and years served. \u00a0There were about 40 names called off and those who were present stood and were applauded for their service. \u00a0After the service, the Veterans gathered in the clubhouse for refreshments and a time to talk with others that served.<\/p>\n<p>We are all blessed to have had these men and women risk, and in some cases give their lives to protect our freedoms. \u00a0This ceremony is just one small way we can give back and let them know their sacrifice has not gone unnoticed or unappreciated.<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-3798 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-large'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.29.18.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.29.18-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-3799\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.29.18-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.29.18-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.29.18-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.29.18.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-3799'>\n\t\t\t\tInstalling the solar light on top of the pole\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.26.25.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.26.25-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-3800\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.26.25-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.26.25-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.26.25-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/06\/2017-06-07-12.26.25.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-3800'>\n\t\t\t\tCarr (Cable TV Truck) came to help by installing the solar light\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herb